[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4116406715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117774#issuecomment-4116406715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117774","id":4116406715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71W2G7","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T08:47:10Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T08:47:10Z","body":"This looks really good overall!\r\n\r\nFor the record I wouldn't squash the commits before merging, this split is useful to keep in the history IMO for clarity.\r\n\r\n> Splits `ResourceFormat*` from `main.h` into `main_resource_format.h` files\r\n\r\nThis goes a bit against the usual naming scheme where we try to name files as the snake case version of the class they define, so `resource_loader_<type>.h` would be a bit more in line with the usual convention. But here I agree that it can make sense to diverge from the convention (which isn't universally applied, if only because we shove multiple classes per files) to have a shared prefix between the resource and its resource loader/save.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4116406715/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4117322850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117774#issuecomment-4117322850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117774","id":4117322850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71aVxi","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T11:07:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T11:08:53Z","body":"Ok, won't squash \n\nRegarding the naming scheme, it does diverge from the `PascalCase` class being in `snake_case.h` file, but as you accurately point out, it was done this way for organizational purposes. \n\nIn my opinion the classes should be renamed if anything, not the files. (They aren't used anywhere except `register_core_types.cpp` and aren't exposed so no compat breakage)\nThe logic to me is (for example) that we have the `JSON` class's `ResourceFormatLoader`, so it ends up being `JSONResourceFormatLoader`. Yes, the parent class is the second half of the name in this case, but I believe it's better to highlight the specialization before the parent class. A good example of that being all the `*Container`classes, where specialization comes first (e.g. `Scroll`-) then parent (-`Container`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4117322850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138829619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117774#issuecomment-4138829619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117774","id":4138829619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72sYcz","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_